00:01:01.727 --> 00:01:05.264
in Austin, Texas, at U.T.

00:01:05.264 --> 00:01:07.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:10.502 --> 00:01:13.072
I have to ask you a few
questions while you're here.

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:14.440
Thank you for being here.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:18.545
You could live anywhere in
the world if you wanted to.

00:01:18.545 --> 00:01:20.813
Why do you choose to
live in Austin?

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:23.749
-Well, first off,
I am a proud Texan.

00:01:23.749 --> 00:01:28.088
[ Cheers and applause ]
I was born in South Texas.

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:30.356
I was raised
in East Texas and, yes,

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:33.259
now I hang my hat
right here in Austin, Texas.

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:35.060
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:38.097
One of the great things about
Austin is to make it here,

00:01:38.097 --> 00:01:41.233
all you really got to do is
be yourself.

00:01:41.233 --> 00:01:42.802
You can be a cowboy,
you can be a hippie,

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:46.039
you can be an American Indian,
an Asian, lesbian,

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:49.375
white, black, brown, yellow,
a blue-haired dwarf,

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:50.776
and you are welcome in Austin.

00:01:50.776 --> 00:01:51.911
-You are, yeah.

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:53.112
-You really are.

00:01:53.112 --> 00:01:56.082
-That's the thing --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:56.082 --> 00:01:58.551
-We got a very lyrical city.

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:01.287
But what I think unites
all that diversity

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:03.623
I was talking about is --
we have a cowboy code

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:07.727
and we have a sense of common
values that we all rally behind.

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:13.833
In Austin, nobody's too good,
but everybody's good enough.

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:17.970
We don't lie, cheat, and steal.
We're an optimistic people.

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:20.840
We're resilient.
We're friendly. We're fair.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.308
We respect and value ourselves

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:25.177
and we respect
and value each other.

00:02:25.177 --> 00:02:29.381
We do not chase lawsuits.
No, we do not chase lawsuits.

00:02:29.381 --> 00:02:33.286
We do break a sweat because we
pay the duty to live here

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:35.054
and we know that living here
and what we have here --

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:36.589
it's not free.

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:38.891
No, no.
That is how we're living here.

00:02:38.891 --> 00:02:44.363
And guess what.
It's a lot cooler because we do.

00:02:44.363 --> 00:02:46.399
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:50.903 --> 00:02:52.204
And y'all know what
I'm talking about.

00:02:52.204 --> 00:02:56.042
To all newcomers -- and we got
125 a day coming here --

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:57.377
alright, if you don't want
to come here

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:59.411
and respect our values
and our tradition

00:02:59.411 --> 00:03:01.714
and our core soul,
please keep on flyin'.

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:05.484
Drive on by.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:05.484 --> 00:03:07.753
-That's right.

00:03:07.753 --> 00:03:10.522
Everyone has been
so awesome to us.

00:03:10.522 --> 00:03:12.992
Not just me, but
my whole crew and everybody.

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:16.362
I mean, people can recognize me,
but everybody, top to bottom,

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:18.698
have been talking about it,
how nice everyone's been to me.

00:03:18.698 --> 00:03:19.766
Like, "Jimmy, you should go
to this place.

00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:20.866
You should go to this place.

00:03:20.866 --> 00:03:22.201
Oh, do you want a beer?
Do you want this?

00:03:22.201 --> 00:03:24.069
Do you want --" I was like,
"Yeah, I do want a beer

00:03:24.069 --> 00:03:25.604
and I do want that."

00:03:25.604 --> 00:03:27.240
But they're like, "You want me
to give you a ride home?"

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.942
I go, "No, I'm good, man.
I'm good, I'm good. Thank you."

00:03:28.942 --> 00:03:30.309
-Yeah.

00:03:30.309 --> 00:03:33.312
-But you walked out here through
a sign that said, "M.O.C."

00:03:33.312 --> 00:03:34.981
-Yes.
-"Minister of Culture."

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:37.250
-Yes, sir.
-What does that mean to you?

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:39.151
-So, alright, as
Minister of Culture,

00:03:39.151 --> 00:03:43.623
I want to champion certain
guiding principles that we have.

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:44.691
Some of them I just spoke of,
you know?

00:03:44.691 --> 00:03:45.758
-Yeah.

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:47.226
-Principles that are the
soul of Austin,

00:03:47.226 --> 00:03:49.929
that are the soul of
the University of Texas.

00:03:49.929 --> 00:03:51.531
We've earned our stripes.
-Yeah.

00:03:51.531 --> 00:03:54.534
-And now we're growing.
We want to grow our heritage.

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:57.170
We need to maintain
and share those same values

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:59.338
as we were growing
and embracing progress.

00:03:59.338 --> 00:04:01.206
-Do you like like
"Keep Austin weird"?

00:04:01.206 --> 00:04:03.476
Is that --
-"Keep Austin weird" is great.

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:04.977
It's been around for decades.
It started --

00:04:04.977 --> 00:04:06.278
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:06.278 --> 00:04:10.449
It started to preserve
small businesses in Austin.

00:04:10.449 --> 00:04:11.483
And it's great,
and I don't think

00:04:11.483 --> 00:04:12.852
it should go anywhere.

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:15.387
I do think, though, that now
that Austin is coming into

00:04:15.387 --> 00:04:18.424
a 2.0 stage, that there's
something that encapsulates

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:20.693
"Keep Austin weird,"
plus a little bit more.

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:23.129
And I think we should remind
ourselves daily

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:28.701
that we need to keep
Austin Austin, as well.

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:32.938
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:04:32.938 --> 00:04:35.574
Now, Jimmy, this city --

00:04:35.574 --> 00:04:37.075
the values that
I'm talking about.

00:04:37.075 --> 00:04:40.179
This city and this university --
I get these values

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:41.947
because this city
and this university

00:04:41.947 --> 00:04:43.415
has shown me those values

00:04:43.415 --> 00:04:45.651
for the last 30 years
of my life here.

00:04:45.651 --> 00:04:48.254
-And now you're a full-on --
You're a professor here...

00:04:48.254 --> 00:04:49.688
-Yes, sir.
-...at the school.

00:04:49.688 --> 00:04:52.024
And you will be teaching
"Script to Screen."

00:04:52.024 --> 00:04:53.125
-Yes, sir.

00:04:53.125 --> 00:04:54.627
-What it is like to be
in a class with

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:56.763
Matthew McConaughey
as a teacher?

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:58.364
-I think it's fun to be
in my class.

00:04:58.364 --> 00:05:00.400
It sure is fun to teach it.
-It is, yeah?

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.733
-Yeah, it's the class I wish
I would've had

00:05:01.733 --> 00:05:03.969
when I was here at film school.

00:05:03.969 --> 00:05:05.771
I noticed, about 15 years ago,
how different

00:05:05.771 --> 00:05:08.707
the final film was from
the original script that I read.

00:05:08.707 --> 00:05:10.543
So what I've done is created
a class that we

00:05:10.543 --> 00:05:12.811
chronologically track
the original script

00:05:12.811 --> 00:05:14.480
all the way through
the first assembly,

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:17.483
all the way through
the final picture in a semester.

00:05:17.483 --> 00:05:19.952
So it's putting
the science behind

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:23.890
the magic of movie-making
for storytellers of tomorrow.

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:25.591
-I want to say
happy belated birthday

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:26.659
to you, my friend.

00:05:26.659 --> 00:05:28.527
You turned 50 years old.
Happy birthday.

00:05:28.527 --> 00:05:30.196
-Yes, sir. Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:30.196 --> 00:05:35.267
-You look pretty good.
You look real good, buddy.

00:05:35.267 --> 00:05:36.702
-It's the company I'm keeping.

00:05:36.702 --> 00:05:38.537
-What I want to talk to
you about is how you celebrated,

00:05:38.537 --> 00:05:40.906
-'cause I think that was --
It meant a lot to me.

00:05:40.906 --> 00:05:42.641
I read about it.
But explain to everybody.

00:05:42.641 --> 00:05:45.010
How did you celebrate your 50th?
Did you have a big party?

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:46.345
-I spent time with my family.

00:05:46.345 --> 00:05:50.082
We also -- Myself and
Wild Turkey partnering up

00:05:50.082 --> 00:05:52.218
with Operation BBQ Relief

00:05:52.218 --> 00:05:55.988
and went out to Los Angeles
and served barbecue and food.

00:05:55.988 --> 00:05:58.658
Prepared it and served it
to 20 different firehouses.

00:05:58.658 --> 00:05:59.892
So as they're fighting
the fires out there,

00:05:59.892 --> 00:06:01.360
there's a lot of people
in the front line.

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:02.661
They needed food.

00:06:02.661 --> 00:06:04.296
They needed to put food
in the freezer.

00:06:04.296 --> 00:06:05.998
So we went out and said --
gave them a "howdy"

00:06:05.998 --> 00:06:08.000
and helped them out.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.334
-I love that you do that.

00:06:09.334 --> 00:06:10.503
I love that you give back.

00:06:10.503 --> 00:06:12.171
You don't forget
where you came from.

00:06:12.171 --> 00:06:14.039
And now you're teaching here
and you're doing that.

00:06:14.039 --> 00:06:17.676
But one of the other big
milestones in your life is --

00:06:17.676 --> 00:06:20.445
you joined Instagram
a couple days ago.

00:06:20.445 --> 00:06:24.983
-Yes, on my birthday.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:24.983 --> 00:06:27.019
-Would you be kind enough
to take a selfie

00:06:27.019 --> 00:06:29.354
with me and this
great crowd right now?

00:06:29.354 --> 00:06:30.389
-Come on.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:30.389 --> 00:06:32.758
-Yeah, I'll do it.
-Go Down there.

00:06:32.758 --> 00:06:36.395
Down there, Matt.
-♪ I'll follow you ♪

00:06:36.395 --> 00:06:41.767
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:06:41.767 --> 00:06:44.636
-Alright, here we go.

00:06:44.636 --> 00:06:46.906
Alright, here we go.

00:06:46.906 --> 00:06:48.174
Alright, we got to
look this way.

00:06:48.174 --> 00:06:49.575
-Alright, alright.
-You're facing the wrong way.

00:06:49.575 --> 00:06:50.976
Alright?

00:06:50.976 --> 00:06:53.379
Alright, this is controlled
chaos is what we call this.

00:06:53.379 --> 00:06:54.413
All right, ready? Oh, wait.

00:06:54.413 --> 00:06:57.450
We got to be -- One, two, three.

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:59.452
[ Cheers and applause ]

